{
  "_readme": [
    "The machine-readable form of refs/EXTENSION_CONFORMANCE.md sections 1.3, 1.4 and 1.5:",
    "every extension API member Orbit is known NOT to have.",
    "",
    "OrbitTests/ExtensionSchemaConformanceTests.swift diffs Orbit's own schemas",
    "(Chromium/Embedder/common/api/*.json) against the vendored upstream snapshot in",
    "OrbitTests/Fixtures/UpstreamAPISchemas/ and asserts the delta is EXACTLY this file.",
    "",
    "That means the test fails in both directions, on purpose:",
    "  - a member that disappears from Orbit and appears here is a regression;",
    "  - a member that Orbit IMPLEMENTS also fails, until someone deletes it from",
    "    this file. Updating the file is the deliberate act that records the win.",
    "A fixture-based test can only check members its author thought to write down;",
    "this is the only check in the suite that can detect ABSENCE.",
    "",
    "Regenerate with:  Scripts/extension-schemas sync && Scripts/extension-schemas update-expectations",
    "Then READ THE DIFF. Notes and reasons are preserved across regeneration.",
    "",
    "reason, on an absent namespace:",
    "  notPorted       chrome-layer, in scope, Orbit has not ported it (section 1.4)",
    "  outOfScope      ChromeOS hardware/shell, enterprise, or the Chrome Apps model",
    "                  Orbit does not host (section 1.5)",
    "  chromeInternal  allowlist-only; no third-party extension can reach it",
    "  unclassified    a new Chromium added it and nobody has triaged it yet -- the",
    "                  test rejects this value, so the bump forces the triage",
    "",
    "neverDispatchedEvents: events Orbit DECLARES in a schema and never fires. These are",
    "invisible to a schema diff -- the member is present -- and are the failure mode",
    "OrbitTests/Fixtures/EventLiveness.json plus ChromiumExtensionEventLivenessLiveTests",
    "exist to catch. An event listed here must also be listed as notDispatched there."
  ],
